1
00:05:35,454 --> 00:05:41,454
Two worlds. One home.

2
00:11:10,909 --> 00:11:16,909
Warcraft is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by Duncan Jones.

3
00:16:46,363 --> 00:16:52,363
The peaceful realm of Azeroth stands on the brink of war as its civilization faces a fearsome
race of invaders: orc warriors fleeing their dying home to colonize another.

4
00:22:21,818 --> 00:22:27,818
As a portal opens to connect the two worlds, one army faces
destruction and the other faces extinction.

5
00:27:57,272 --> 00:28:03,272
From opposing sides, two heroes are set on a collision course that will
decide the fate of their family, their people, and their home.

6
00:33:32,727 --> 00:33:38,727
Commander Anduin Lothar, played by Travis Fimmel.

7
00:39:08,181 --> 00:39:14,181
Garona Halforcen, played by Paula Patton.

8
00:44:43,636 --> 00:44:49,636
Medivh (Guardian), played by Ben Foster.

9
00:50:19,090 --> 00:50:25,090
King Llane Wrynn, played by Dominic Cooper.

10
00:55:54,545 --> 00:56:00,545
Khadgar, played by Ben Schnetzer.

11
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
Durotan / Antonidas, played by Toby Kebbell.

12
01:07:05,454 --> 01:07:11,454
Warcraft  (alternatively known as Warcraft: The Beginning) is a 2016 American
action fantasy film based on the video game series of the same name.

13
01:12:40,909 --> 01:12:46,909
Directed by Duncan Jones, who co-wrote with Charles Leavitt, it stars Travis Fimmel, Paula Patton, Ben
Foster, Dominic Cooper, Toby Kebbell, Ben Schnetzer, Robert Kazinsky, and Daniel Wu.

14
01:18:16,363 --> 01:18:22,363
The film follows Anduin Lothar of Stormwind and Durotan of the Frostwolf clan as heroes set on opposite sides of
a growing war, as the warlock Gul'dan leads the Horde to invade Azeroth using a magic portal.

15
01:23:51,818 --> 01:23:57,818
Together, a few human heroes and dissenting Orcs must attempt to
stop the true evil behind this war and restore peace.

16
01:29:27,272 --> 01:29:33,272
The film was first announced in 2006 as a project partnership between
Legendary Pictures and the game's developer, Blizzard Entertainment.

17
01:35:02,727 --> 01:35:08,727
Warcraft premiered in Paris on May 24, 2016, and was released by
Universal Pictures in the United States on June 10, 2016.

18
01:40:38,181 --> 01:40:44,181
The film grossed $439 million worldwide against a production budget of $160 million,
becoming the highest-grossing film based on a video game at the time.

19
01:46:13,636 --> 01:46:19,636
However, it failed to reach its break-even point of $450–500
million after global marketing and distribution.

20
01:51:49,090 --> 01:51:55,090
The film received generally negative reviews from critics, though
fans of the Warcraft franchise were kinder to it.

21
01:57:24,545 --> 01:57:30,545
The film explores themes of elves, dwarf, magic, betrayal, king.
